# R2 bidirectionality verification — Stage 8 / Phase 0 (hygiene: #28 + #34)

Per the R2 rule: for each distinct behavior a new test pins, mutate the
implementation to break exactly that behavior, run vitest, and record the
GENUINE failure (proving the test discriminates real behavior, not a
tautology). Every mutation was reverted immediately (`git checkout`); the
working tree returned clean after each. Baseline before this work: 567 tests;
after (additive #28 + #34 tests): 575 tests, all green.

Commands run from the worktree:
`/home/subzerodev/workspace/satisfactory-foundry/.worktrees/planner-p0`.

---

## #28 — null-prototype catalog maps

### B1 — parse boundary seeds null-proto (docs-loader)

Mutation: revert the `items` seed in `parseDocsJson` from
`Object.create(null)` back to a plain `{}` literal.

Test: `npx vitest run src/data/docs-loader.test.ts -t "null-prototype maps resist"`

Genuine FAIL:

```
 ❯ src/data/docs-loader.test.ts (27 tests | 2 failed | 24 skipped)
   × misses cleanly on an absent id — no lookup resolves an Object.prototype member
   × builds all three maps with a null prototype
 FAIL  src/data/docs-loader.test.ts > parseDocsJson — null-prototype maps resist prototype-key collision (#28) > misses cleanly on an absent id — no lookup resolves an Object.prototype member
 FAIL  src/data/docs-loader.test.ts > parseDocsJson — null-prototype maps resist prototype-key collision (#28) > builds all three maps with a null prototype
      Tests  2 failed | 1 passed | 24 skipped (27)
```

The plain-`{}` seed makes `cat.items["nonexistent"]` resolve
`Object.prototype`'s `constructor` function (and fails the null-proto
assertion) — exactly the collision the fix prevents.

### B2 — revive boundary re-nulls after structured clone (catalog-store)

Mutation: revert the `items` rebuild in `reviveCatalog` from
`Object.create(null)` back to a plain `{}` literal.

Test: `npx vitest run src/data/catalog-store.test.ts -t "null-prototype maps survive revive"`

Genuine FAIL:

```
 ❯ src/data/catalog-store.test.ts (10 tests | 1 failed | 9 skipped)
   × revived items/machines/recipes maps have a null prototype
 FAIL  src/data/catalog-store.test.ts > catalog cache — null-prototype maps survive revive (#28) > revived items/machines/recipes maps have a null prototype
      Tests  1 failed | 9 skipped (10)
```

IDB structured clone yields plain-proto objects; without the re-null on
revive the loaded catalog's maps carry `Object.prototype` again. The
save→load round-trip test pins the second build boundary independently of
the parse boundary.

