## #34 — planForLink resolver

All #34 mutations target `src/ui/graph-flow.ts` (`planForLink`) and run
`npx vitest run src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts -t "planForLink"`.

### B3 — null EXACTLY when the item is missing

Mutation: change the missing-item guard from `return null` to
`return { kind: "unsolved", mode: "belt" }` (a non-null plan).

Genuine FAIL:

```
   × returns null EXACTLY when the item is missing from the catalog
 FAIL  src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts > planForLink (#34) > returns null EXACTLY when the item is missing from the catalog
      Tests  1 failed | 3 passed | 29 skipped (33)
```

### B4 — an unsolved rate flows THROUGH as { kind: "unsolved" }, never null

Mutation: add `const r = linkRequiredRate(...); if (r === null) return null;`
before the `computeLinkTransport` call (the v1 defect the r1 reviewers
caught — null-on-unsolved erases the inspector's "solve both stages to size
the fleet" line).

Genuine FAIL:

```
   × passes an unsolved rate THROUGH as { kind: 'unsolved' }, never null
 FAIL  src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts > planForLink (#34) > passes an unsolved rate THROUGH as { kind: 'unsolved' }, never null
      Tests  1 failed | 3 passed | 29 skipped (33)
```

### B5 — the belt default resolves (null-on-belt would erase the belt fleet lines)

Mutation: add `if (link.transport === undefined) return null;` before the
`computeLinkTransport` call (the belt-erasing defect the design boundary
forbids).

Genuine FAIL:

```
   × resolves the belt default for an absent-transport link (not null)
 FAIL  src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts > planForLink (#34) > resolves the belt default for an absent-transport link (not null)
      Tests  1 failed | 3 passed | 29 skipped (33)
```

### B6 — a configured mode resolves identically to the hand-built preamble

Mutation: pass a hard-coded `{ mode: "belt" }` in place of the link's own
`link.transport`, so the resolved plan's `kind` diverges (continuous vs the
vehicle plan the preamble builds).

Genuine FAIL:

```
   × resolves a vehicle mode identically to the hand-built preamble
 FAIL  src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts > planForLink (#34) > resolves a vehicle mode identically to the hand-built preamble
      Tests  1 failed | 3 passed | 29 skipped (33)
```

Note (recorded honesty): a FIRST B6 attempt — scaling the rate by 2× inside
planForLink — did NOT fail this test, because the fixture's 600/min demand
fits one truck at both 600 and 1200/min, so the vehicle plan is identical.
The passing (non-)FAIL was rejected and the mutation replaced with the
transport-mode override above, which discriminates cleanly. The equality
assertion IS sensitive to the transport arg (the load-bearing part of the
fold), just not to a rate scaling small enough to round to the same fleet.

